ey features:**\n- **Concurrency limit**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to ensure at most `max_concurrent` tasks run simultaneously\n- **Cleanup on interrupt**: When KeyboardInterrupt occurs, it cancels all tasks and waits for their cleanup code (finally blocks, context managers) to complete before re-raising the exception\n- **Clean API**: Importable as `from run import run_tasks` with the exact signature you requested\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Creates all async tasks upfront with the semaphore wrapper\n2. Waits for all tasks using `asyncio.gather`\n3. If interrupted, explicitly cancels each task and waits for cleanup to run before propagating the KeyboardInterrupt\n\nI verified it works with tests that confirmed:\n- Concurrency limit enforcement (max 2 concurrent when running 6 tasks)\n- All cleanup code executes even on keyboard interrupt","ttft_ms":24036,"type":"result","duration_ms":68471,"uuid":"2758573b-d8f0-4fb0-9063-7de29dc4dda8","ttft_stream_ms":1075,"time_to_request_ms":80,"queued_turn_count":0}
